2995. Viewers Turned Streamers
Table: Sessions
Column Name	Type
user_id	int
session_id	int
session_type	enum
session_date	date

There is no primary key for this table.

Each row represents a user’s session on a given date.

session_type is an enum with values:

'Viewer'

'Streamer'

Definition

A user is considered a viewer turned streamer if:

The user has at least one Viewer session, and

The user has at least one Streamer session, and

The user’s first Streamer session happens after their first Viewer session.

Task

Write an SQL query to find the user_id(s) of all viewers turned streamers.

Return the result table in any order.

Example
Input

Sessions

user_id	session_id	session_type	session_date
1	101	Viewer	2023-01-01
1	102	Viewer	2023-01-02
1	103	Streamer	2023-01-05
2	201	Streamer	2023-01-01
2	202	Viewer	2023-01-03
3	301	Viewer	2023-01-02
Output
user_id
1

Solution 1
===========
SELECT
  user_id
FROM Sessions
GROUP BY user_id
HAVING
  MIN(CASE WHEN session_type = 'Viewer'   THEN session_date END) IS NOT NULL
  AND MIN(CASE WHEN session_type = 'Streamer' THEN session_date END) IS NOT NULL
  AND MIN(CASE WHEN session_type = 'Streamer' THEN session_date END)
      > MIN(CASE WHEN session_type = 'Viewer' THEN session_date END);

Solution 2
============
SELECT v.user_id
FROM (
  SELECT user_id, MIN(session_date) AS first_view
  FROM Sessions
  WHERE session_type = 'Viewer'
  GROUP BY user_id
) v
JOIN (
  SELECT user_id, MIN(session_date) AS first_stream
  FROM Sessions
  WHERE session_type = 'Streamer'
  GROUP BY user_id
) s
  ON v.user_id = s.user_id
WHERE s.first_stream > v.first_view;

Solution 3
===========
WITH ranked AS (
  SELECT
    user_id,
    session_type,
    session_date,
    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
      PARTITION BY user_id, session_type
      ORDER BY session_date
    ) AS rn
  FROM Sessions
),
firsts AS (
  SELECT
    user_id,
    MAX(CASE WHEN session_type = 'Viewer' AND rn = 1 THEN session_date END) AS first_view,
    MAX(CASE WHEN session_type = 'Streamer' AND rn = 1 THEN session_date END) AS first_stream
  FROM ranked
  GROUP BY user_id
)
SELECT user_id
FROM firsts
WHERE first_view IS NOT NULL
  AND first_stream IS NOT NULL
  AND first_stream > first_view;

Solution 4
============
SELECT DISTINCT s1.user_id
FROM Sessions s1
WHERE s1.session_type = 'Viewer'
  AND EXISTS (
    SELECT 1
    FROM Sessions s2
    WHERE s2.user_id = s1.user_id
      AND s2.session_type = 'Streamer'
      AND s2.session_date > s1.session_date
  );
